      "writtenOn": "2020-03-04T19:38:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s cleaner to define UINT16_MAX for the kernel. All other  projects importing ec_commands.h include stdint.h, where UINT*_MAX are defined. That is,\n\n  #ifdef __KERNEL__\n  #define UINT16_MAX U16_MAX\n  #endif\n\nDo the kernel reviewers specifically request not to define UINT16_MAX? If so, why?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
