        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-04T22:09:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see several files define UINT16_MAX under kernel v4.14. linux/lib/libfdt_env.h also defines UINT32_MAX. So, we\u0027re not going to be the first who defines an integer max/min macro:\n\n  #ifndef UINT16_MAX\n  #define UINT16_MAX ((u16)(~0U))\n  #endif\n\n\u003e it has to look stock\n\nOr can we make make_linux_ec_commands_h.sh substitute UINT16_MAX with U16_MAX?\n\nIf we define macro X because the kernel doesn\u0027t like an alternative (and standard) macro Y, we\u0027ll gradually taint the namespace and lose the readability. Foreign projects have to accept such macros too.",
      "parentUuid": "8f685eb1_6fc7da6c",
